{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5iv47pwrypikmdlj6kum7qmg5dmj7mibpx6jc7yrb6yruq744kua","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass; three real divergences were found and fixed in the Rust.\n\n## What the code is\n`c_src/src/main.c` is a 17-line program: `driver(s1,s2)` prints `strcspn(s1,s2)` with `\"%zu\\n\"`; `main` reads two lines with `fgets` into 100-byte buffers, unconditionally chops the last byte of each (`s[strlen(s)-1]='\\0'`, which underflows to index `-1` for empty strings), then calls `driver`.\n\n## Phase A — surface mapped\n| artifact | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | C `.so` exports exactly `driver`, `main`; Rust `.so` now exports both. Symbol diff **empty**, no undefined non-libc symbols. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | **27 rows**, derived mechanically (the C has *no* `if`/`assert`/error return — all rejection is implicit in `fgets`/`strlen`/the 100-byte buffers/the OOB write). |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | **35 rows**. Build config: **1** combination only — `[features]` is empty, `CMakeLists.txt` has no options, the C has no `#ifdef`. |\n\nStructural work: `src/core.rs` (translated logic) shared by `src/main.rs` (bin) and a new `src/lib.rs` `cdylib` exporting `driver` + `main`; `examples/so_runner.rs` dlopens either `.so` with `libloading` and calls only its exported symbols; `verify.sh` automates every combination, both profiles, and cross-checks that every table row names a test that really ran (and that no test is missing from the tables).\n\n## Divergences found and fixed (C is ground truth)\n1. **NULL/invalid pointer to `driver`** — C dies with SIGSEGV(11); Rust's debug assertions turned the plain `*p` deref into a `panic!`/SIGABRT(6). Fixed with `read_volatile` for the C-string scan → SIGSEGV in both debug and release.\n2. **Broken stdout pipe** — the C exe is killed by SIGPIPE(13); Rust's runtime pre-sets `SIGPIPE` to `SIG_IGN` so it exited 0. Fixed by restoring `SIG_DFL` in the bin's `main` (the `.so` deliberately does *not*, matching the C `.so`).\n3. **Repeated `main()` calls in one process** — the extra `BufReader` wrapper discarded read-ahead data that C's `FILE*` stdin keeps. Fixed by reading through the global `StdinLock` buffer.\n\nAlso fixed: `#[no_mangle] main` clashed with cargo's unit-test harness entry point (`cfg(not(test))`).\n\n## Results\n- `cargo test`: **67 tests pass** (35 Phase B + 28 Phase C + 4 Phase D) in **both debug and release**; `cargo check --no-default-features` clean.\n- Harness sensitivity proven by mutation testing: disabled chop, off-by-one `fgets` cap, inverted `strcspn`, signed-char comparison, missing newline stop, format change, defensive NULL check, removed SIGPIPE restore — **all detected**. (Only equivalent mutant: the provably unreachable `strlen` fallback.)\n- Nothing in `c_src/` was modified (`main.c` md5 unchanged; only the CMake `build/` dir was created, as instructed)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1173,"cache_read_input_tokens":184732,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1173,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a291d035-71b4-4cd6-8451-4f311646a55d","uuid":"c6e60f84-6d14-428d-b2d0-c99bed4b7896","timestamp":"2026-08-18T07:05:16.915Z"}
